# Data

## Indexes and search

- Each domain defines and owns its indexes, vector indexes included, in its own schema files.
- Use SurrealDB-native full-text (BM25), vector (HNSW; DiskANN when the corpus exceeds memory, 3.1+), and hybrid (`search::rrf`) before adding another search store.
- Filter inside KNN queries (`<|K,EF|>` with the condition in the query). Never post-filter in application code.
- Check index and query syntax against the docs for the installed SurrealDB version before writing it.

## Embeddings

- Compute in Rust through the platform embedding client. Bedrock in deployed stages. Ollama is allowed locally, behind that client. Domains and apps never call a provider directly.
- Store the model ID and dimension beside every embedding. Changing either is a re-embed task. Never mix in place.
- Hash content so unchanged chunks are not re-embedded.

## Enrichment

- Store inferred or enriched facts apart from source facts, with provenance (source record, method, model and prompt version) and confidence. Never overwrite source facts.
- Cheap deterministic steps (rules, small extractors) before any LLM call.

## Entity resolution

- The domain that owns an entity's identity owns its resolution. Others link by record ID.
- Order: deterministic keys, then candidates (full-text, KNN, and shared graph neighbours, fused), then thresholds (auto-link, review, new), then an LLM only for the ambiguous band.
- Never merge destructively. Write `same_as` edges with confidence and sources. Keep ambiguous matches distinct. Every resolution decision goes to the decision record.

## Database-level tools

- SurrealMCP and embedded MCP: non-production only, read-only where possible, never in `apps/agent` or any production toolset.
- Production agents reach data only through domain MCP tools.

## Gates

`.helmsman/tools/surreal` checks that a schema file is present and that `.helmsman/setup.md` has a Integration command. It does not start the database. `.helmsman/tools/postgres` runs sqlfluff when that binary is installed, and fails when a sqlfluff or migrate config is present and the binary is missing. With neither, it skips and says so. `.helmsman/tools/dynamodb` and `.helmsman/tools/opensearch` validate tracked JSON. None of these call a live service from pre-commit.
